## Goal

Close the missing-band hole exposed by <issue id="36530b59-568d-4890-9183-357e17e25eac" label="RYA-1129" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1129/phase-a-intake-freeze-laboratorygraded-gf-assets-for-every-canonical" />: acquire and verify the **actual Solar C/N/O reference transitions used in the AGSS21 adopted-abundance lineage across FUV, NUV, VIS, red optical, NIR, and IR**, including the molecular indicators CH, C2, CN, NH, OH, and CO.

The committed <issue id="36530b59-568d-4890-9183-357e17e25eac" label="RYA-1129" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1129/phase-a-intake-freeze-laboratorygraded-gf-assets-for-every-canonical" /> manifests are the Codex canonical denominator, not the published Solar numerator. Current gaps are material:

* atomic FUV: zero C/N/O rows in the intake manifests;
* near-UV: C 0, N 1, O 1 atomic rows;
* molecular IR: CO 0 canonical rows; OH 1 VIS-only row;
* CH/C2/CN/NH are overwhelmingly VIS/near-UV and carry insufficient typed source provenance.

This ticket owns source discovery, acquisition, transcription, verification, and cross-reference. <issue id="a89a870e-c3a6-44f3-ade2-0a8937798375" label="RYA-1130" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1130/schema-separate-molecular-transition-provenance-from-atomic-canonical" /> owns the molecular schema. Source acquisition and audit proceed immediately; only final molecular canonicalization is blocked on <issue id="a89a870e-c3a6-44f3-ade2-0a8937798375" label="RYA-1130" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1130/schema-separate-molecular-transition-provenance-from-atomic-canonical" />.

## Authoritative method

Inherit the mandatory “Solar reference-line-set census — AGSS21 lineage, all bands” section of <issue id="f1039187-38b1-463a-98eb-ed3b4e9e7c5e" label="RYA-946" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-946/umbrella-all-element-laboratory-gf-sweep-literature-validation" /> and the <issue id="c0ab6b71-4ad1-4182-8796-f7a80c74b437" label="RYA-1109" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1109/source-create-the-asplund-agss21-solar-fe-line-list-gf-the-reference" /> Fe treatment.

Do not infer “Asplund-used” from familiar wavelengths or from the final abundance. For each C/N/O adopted value:

1. read AGSS21 and identify the exact element-specific source analysis;
2. follow the citations to primary paper, supplement, CDS/VizieR/ExoMol/MARCS/Turbospectrum asset, or author table;
3. transcribe the used and explicitly rejected transitions;
4. validate extraction by published counts/means/identities where the paper permits;
5. crossmatch to Codex on physical transition identity, never wavelength alone.

## Required source scope

### Atomic

* C I/C II and any UV ion/forbidden indicators actually used in the adopted Solar lineage;
* N I/N II and relevant UV/IR indicators;
* O I/\[O I\]/O II and relevant UV/IR indicators;
* blend components that materially enter a Solar indicator, including Ni I at \[O I\] 6300;
* all source-used bands, including negative published band selections.

### Molecular

Keep independent source lineages for:

* C: CH, C2, CN, CO;
* N: CN, NH;
* O: OH, CO;
* isotopologues where used or supplied.

Acquire exact transition-data release/table/version plus DOI/ADS/catalogue identifier, wavelength convention, isotopologue/component normalization, partition-function source, dissociation-energy source, license, and retrieval metadata. Do not equate a VALD delivery label with primary molecular provenance.

## Machine-readable output

One row per published-used or explicitly rejected transition:

`reference_line_set | adopted_solar_value_lineage | source_paper/table/catalog | use_status | species/isotopologue | transition_identity | wavelength | medium | EP/energies | published_loggf | published_gf_source | EW/profile/weight | source_band | canonical_line_id | Codex_loggf | Codex_gf_tier | Codex_nist_grade | Codex_lab_source | Codex_sigma | Codex_DOI | delta_loggf | join_status | ambiguity_note`

Also emit:

* per-band coverage matrix: used, rejected, Codex-matched, graded, ungraded, absent, ambiguous;
* source/provenance manifest with checksums and retrieval dates;
* source-lineage report showing how each set contributes to AGSS21's adopted C/N/O values;
* explicit `SOURCE_LINE_LIST_NOT_PUBLISHED` findings only after primary sources and supplements/catalogues are checked.

## Gates

- [ ] Every AGSS21 C/N/O adopted value traced to its line-level source(s).
- [ ] All source-used FUV/NUV/VIS/red-optical/NIR/IR bands represented.
- [ ] Atomic and molecular lineages remain distinct.
- [ ] CO and OH IR gaps explicitly closed or proven unpublished/unavailable.
- [ ] Zero silent wavelength-only matches.
- [ ] Zero unresolved ambiguous matches in any adopted set.
- [ ] Codex comparison distinguishes used+graded, used+ungraded, graded-not-used, absent, rejected.
- [ ] No abundance derived or gf tuned.
- [ ] Molecular canonicalization uses the ratified <issue id="a89a870e-c3a6-44f3-ade2-0a8937798375" label="RYA-1130" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1130/schema-separate-molecular-transition-provenance-from-atomic-canonical" /> schema.

## Sequencing

1. Begin source tracing/acquisition now.
2. Merge <issue id="36530b59-568d-4890-9183-357e17e25eac" label="RYA-1129" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1129/phase-a-intake-freeze-laboratorygraded-gf-assets-for-every-canonical" />/PR 477 as the baseline denominator.
3. Land <issue id="a89a870e-c3a6-44f3-ade2-0a8937798375" label="RYA-1130" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1130/schema-separate-molecular-transition-provenance-from-atomic-canonical" /> molecular schema.
4. Canonicalize molecular assets and complete the joins.
5. Return the frozen-ready verdict to <issue id="36530b59-568d-4890-9183-357e17e25eac" label="RYA-1129" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-1129/phase-a-intake-freeze-laboratorygraded-gf-assets-for-every-canonical" /> and <issue id="f1039187-38b1-463a-98eb-ed3b4e9e7c5e" label="RYA-946" href="https://linear.app/ryans-adventure-zone/issue/RYA-946/umbrella-all-element-laboratory-gf-sweep-literature-validation" />.

comments.body:
Final intake closeout

PR #487 merged as `bf913e4eefe59e9de3b1a0ec2c610936180540d9` with required CI passing.

Delivered:
- complete 408-row Amarsi et al. (2021) molecular abundance-feature census;
- official C₂, CH, CN, NH, OH, CO, and Barklem–Collet primary holdings;
- 457,814 parsed primary transitions;
- 390/408 exact or explicitly summed physical identities;
- UV/NUV through IR coverage and rejected-indicator ledger;
- complete five-line Amarsi et al. (2020) / AGSS21 N I census;
- checksummed bibliography, molecular constants, conflict, coverage, and crossmatch ledgers;
- no wavelength-only joins, abundance derivation, or gf tuning.

Gate reconciliation:
- nine rounded component sets, five source-release strength differences, and four OH source inconsistencies remain explicit review/fallback rows;
- none of those 18 rows is silently promoted into the measurement-ready adopted set;
- therefore the source intake is complete as `FROZEN_WITH_DOCUMENTED_FALLBACKS` / `INTAKE_COMPLETE_REVIEW_REQUIRED`, while measurement readiness remains withheld for those rows.

RYA-1130 and RYA-1136 are Done. The stale RYA-1130 blocker relation is cleared.
